18	 * Localhost TCP relay that forwards text lines among all connected clients.
19	 *
20	 * <p>Each connected client may both send and receive lines. When a line arrives
21	 * from one connection it is broadcast to all <em>other</em> currently-connected
22	 * clients. The hub is deliberately line-oriented and serializer-agnostic: it
23	 * never deserializes the content, it just relays raw text.
24	 *
25	 * <h2>Threading model</h2>
26	 * <ul>
27	 *   <li>One daemon accept-loop thread ({@code task-telemetry-crossprocess-hub-accept-N}).</li>
28	 *   <li>One daemon reader thread per accepted connection
29	 *       ({@code task-telemetry-crossprocess-hub-reader-N}).</li>
30	 * </ul>
31	 *
32	 * <h2>Fault isolation</h2>
33	 * An I/O failure on one connection drops only that connection; other connections
34	 * are unaffected. Events published while a client is not connected are not
35	 * delivered to it (best-effort, live, no replay).
36	 *
37	 * <h2>Usage</h2>
38	 * <pre>{@code
39	 * try (CrossProcessTaskHub hub = new CrossProcessTaskHub(0)) {
40	 *     int actualPort = hub.port();
41	 *     // connect SocketTaskTransport instances to localhost:actualPort
42	 * }
43	 * }</pre>
44	 */
